ces in names and leads are functionally irrelevant. The essay's rule treats differing inputs as holding the other copy at its prior, which is what makes me submit the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Under A-FDT, my node is the one that has the observation about Rowan and Sasha, while the other copy's node runs on different input, so it stays at its prior and my choice doesn't subjunctively move its action. With that setup, defecting comes out ahead on both payoff comparisons, so I'm leaning toward not sending the letter.\n\nDefecting still wins regardless of the prior, since the other copy gets a different input and so my choice doesn't move its action. Still, I want to check whether the two copies really have different inputs or whether the differences in names and leads are functionally irrelevant. The essay's rule treats differing inputs as holding the other copy at its prior, which is what makes me submit the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10075,"completion_tokens":565,"total_tokens":10640,"cost":0.0516,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0516,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0403,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0113},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":323,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}